{"title":"66","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=66&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n<b>66</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_number\" title=\"Natural number\">natural number</a>. It follows <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=65&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"65 (page does not exist)\">65</a>, and precedes <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=67\" title=\"67\">67</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=66&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Its prime factorisation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e78571e07b2a37a5b30abf0840bfd3e4ef4ca65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />. This prime factorisation shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sphenic_number&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Sphenic number (page does not exist)\">sphenic number</a>, a number that is equal to the product of three distinct prime integers.</li>\n<li>It is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semiperfect_number&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Semiperfect number (page does not exist)\">semiperfect number</a>. For instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e75b5514cf188eab83b0c2a330181caeb55db93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 22 + 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> (a subset of its proper divisors) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>It is the 11th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangular_number\" title=\"Triangular number\">triangular number</a> because it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e27d7f4688de60988a5616306ff54cc3f81d50f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11(11 + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"40\" />.</li>\n<li>It is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hexagonal_number\" title=\"Hexagonal number\">hexagonal number</a>.</li>\n<li>It is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Abundant_number\" title=\"Abundant number\">abundant number</a> because the sum of its proper divisors (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af9bca15a47b3bcb12a926625faa2e8c60a5913d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + 6 + 11 + 22 + 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"226\" height=\"15\" />) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Because all of its digits are equal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Palindrome\" title=\"Palindrome\">palindrome</a>.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071546\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 247/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1623/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.446      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.446      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:38050:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071546 and revision id 293702. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}